Workload breakdown — 4 pods, cluster-wide
 BUCKET                PODS   CPU REQ   CPU USE   MEM REQ   MEM USE   DISK REQ   DISK USE 
 platform              1      100m      3m        128Mi     20Mi      0          512Ki    
 integrated services   1      250m      3m        512Mi     20Mi      0          512Ki    
 applications          1      50m       3m        64Mi      20Mi      0          512Ki    
 other                 1      25m       3m        32Mi      20Mi      0          512Ki    
 TOTAL                 4      425m      12m       736Mi     80Mi      0          2.0Mi    

SCHEDULABLE is allocatable − requested: what a new pod could still ask for.
FREE is allocatable − in-use: what is unused right now. A node can be fully requested
and barely used, or barely requested and full; these two columns are what tells them apart.

Disk is `ephemeral-storage` — the node's root filesystem. The node's IN-USE is the whole
filesystem (OS, container images, logs and volume data included), so it is larger than the
DISK USE column, which counts only each pod's writable layer, logs and emptyDir volumes.

`other` is not empty: 1 pod(s) matched no bucket, in namespace(s) skunkworks.
That is either a workload the platform did not create, or this build's classifier is behind
the cluster — please report the latter.
